@@ -692,6 +696,38 @@ The driver has its own COM identity: CLSID
 `HKCU\Software\ASIO\PipeASIO`, and DLL filename `pipeasio64.dll`. That is why
 it coexists with WineASIO: neither overrides the other.
 
+### Trace points
+
+The ELF driver half `pipeasio64.dll.so` carries six static USDT trace points
+under the provider `pipeasio`. Each one is a 5-byte `nop` plus an ELF note, so
+it costs nothing until a tracer attaches a uprobe to a chosen process; the
+probes are always compiled in and need no setting.
+`readelf -n lib/wine/x86_64-unix/pipeasio64.dll.so` lists them and
+`bpftrace -l 'usdt:/path/to/pipeasio64.dll.so:pipeasio:*'` attaches to them.
+The optional WoW64 unixlib `pipeasio32.so` (`-DBUILD_WOW64_32=ON`, default
+OFF) carries only `cycle_start` and `cycle_end`: the block markers live in
+`src/asio.c`, which the WoW64 build compiles only into the mingw PE front end
+`pipeasio32.dll`, where `PIPEASIO_PROBE` is a no-op.
+
+| Probe | Arguments | Site |
+|---|---|---|
+| `cycle_start` | `clock_nsec, next_nsec, duration, position, flags` | PipeWire process cycle entry (`spa_io_clock` fields) |
+| `cycle_end` | `missed, delivered` | cycle exit: `clock.position` gap before this cycle, host consumed it |
+| `block_start` | `seq, nframes, rate, clock_nsec, deadline_ns, flags` | host gate answered; `flags`: 1 admitted, 2 time info, 4 muted |
+| `block_before_live` / `block_after_live` | `seq` | immediately around the host's `bufferSwitch` |
+| `block_end` | `seq, flags, missed` | every output published |
+
+`seq` counts the blocks of a driver instance from 1. `deadline_ns` is
+PipeWire's `clock.next_nsec` (or the cycle start plus one quantum), in
+CLOCK_MONOTONIC nanoseconds like every other time here: a block whose
+`block_end` lands after it was late, and the graph ran the next cycle without
+it. The data-loop thread is named `pipeasio-rt` and the lifecycle worker
+`pipeasio-worker` (`/proc/<pid>/task/<tid>/comm`), so a tracer can tell them
+apart. The 32-bit mingw front end has no trace points. `include/pipeasio_probe.h`
+is the contract; `include/sdt.h` is the vendored systemtap header (CC0) with
+the x86-64 probe site widened to a 5-byte `nop` so recent kernels can use their
+optimized uprobe path.
+
 ### Testing
 
 `ctest --test-dir build` runs the Linux-native unit and contract tests plus the
